20260529.121102.870 [>kpop..........] # Definition: KPop
20260529.121102.870 [>kpop..........] 
20260529.121102.870 [>kpop..........] [
20260529.121102.870 [>kpop..........] KPop is short for "Karl Popper".
20260529.121102.870 [>kpop..........] You may or may not be solving a repo coding problem, so the Repo Coding Rules may or may not apply.
20260529.121102.870 [>kpop..........] KPop may be referenced later on like a command, "KPop: <problem statement or question>"
20260529.121102.870 [>kpop..........] ]
20260529.121102.870 [>kpop..........] 
20260529.121102.870 [>kpop..........] Apply this method to the user's problem.
20260529.121102.870 [>kpop..........] 
20260529.121102.870 [>kpop..........] Restate the problem clearly.
20260529.121102.870 [>kpop..........] 
20260529.121102.871 [>kpop..........] Repeat until you think you've solved the problem:
20260529.121102.871 [>kpop..........] LOOP_START
20260529.121102.871 [>kpop..........] 
20260529.121102.871 [>kpop..........] - **Brainstorm**: To get fresh, creative ideas, run `malvin invent IDEAS_PROMPT`, where you specify the `IDEAS_PROMPT`. Call this on at least one iteration, but don't wait until the end when it's too late to make use of the ideas.
20260529.121102.871 [>kpop..........]   		  It should take no more than 30s to return, so don't worry about the time. It'll be a worthwhile investment. Use the ideas to help generate new hypotheses.
20260529.121102.871 [>kpop..........] - **Hypothesize**: Hypothesize one falsifiable explanation of the cause of the problem.
20260529.121102.871 [>kpop..........] - **Predict**: Define a falsifying test. If the hypothesis were true, what outcome would the test produce?
20260529.121102.871 [>kpop..........] - **Falsify**: Run the test. If falsified, reject the hypothesis.
20260529.121102.871 [>kpop..........] 
20260529.121102.871 [>kpop..........] LOOP_END
20260529.121102.871 [>kpop..........] 
20260529.121102.871 [>kpop..........] Log your hypotheses and test results -- as they become available -- to `./.malvin/logs/20260529_155928_xk6wud44/_kpop/exp_log_20260529_155928_xk6wud44_g2.md`. Be sure to log hypotheses and results
20260529.121102.871 [>kpop..........] as generate them. They are valuable. The user and other agents will want to read them.
20260529.121102.871 [>kpop..........] 
20260529.121102.871 [>kpop..........] When you are all done, append a brief executive summary and a super-brief tl;dr to the log, and echo both to the user (the chat/context) directly.
